# generated by scripts/golden/gen_config.py from eval/golden/golden_metrics.py; do not edit
# metric: l_plan_format
"""Golden-eval metrics for the v10 pipeline (docs/eval/GOLDEN_EVALS_SPEC.md v1.1, section 7).

One function per metric of the 7.2 registry, m_<name>(instance) -> {"score": float, "explanation": json string of
{"applicable": bool, "detail": ...}}. Scores are never None (agents-cli counts None as an error): a case a metric does
not apply to scores 0.0 with applicable false, and scripts/golden/summary.py leaves it out of every statistic.

Constraints (spec 7.1, gotcha 2): stdlib only, Python 3.8 syntax, no module-level side effects, no sibling imports.
scripts/golden/gen_config.py pastes this whole source into eval/golden/metrics/<name>.py and appends
    def evaluate(instance):
        return _score("<name>", instance)
because agents-cli 1.7.0 execs a custom_function_file into a fresh dict: no __file__, __name__ == "builtins", and
sys.path[0] is its own bin dir, so nothing next to the file can be imported.

The instance (gotcha 3) holds agent_data, eval_case_id, response (= responses[0].response), reference, and the case's
extra fields, here the golden block of spec 6.2 (suite, live_agents, status, crash_class, final_patch, run, llm_calls,
exec_checks, gold_files, gold_functions, ...). Missing and None fields are treated alike (agents-cli drops None).

Terms (spec 7.1):
  stage-run    a maximal run of consecutive events by one author (events authored "tool" do not break it)
  live events  the events of each golden.live_agents agent inside its FIRST stage-run
  live calls   golden.llm_calls records with live true and served upstream | oracle | null
The X definitions port scripts/replay_l4.py (parsed_invented, unparsed_invented, helper_shell, malformed, cant_open);
tests/test_golden_metrics.py checks agreement on every r2_v10_1 trace and that the copied constants still match.
"""
